<h3>Printing work</h3>
<p>As you work through your Lean Organisation Management Techniques course, it might prove useful to print some pages to keep for future reference.</p>
<ol>
<li>Go to the web page you want to print</li>
<li>From the top menu, select <strong>File</strong> and then <strong>Print</strong>.</li>
<li>A print box will appear, in this select the <strong>Preferences</strong> button.</li>
<li>Click on the Paper tab and then click to select <strong>Landscape</strong>. <strong>Once you have done this, click OK</strong>.</li>
<li>Once you're satisfied with your print format, select <strong>Print</strong> to send the page to your printer.</li>
</ol>
<!-- TODO: Update font size increase instructions -->
<h3>Altering the font size</h3>
<p>If you use Internet Explorer, you can change the size of the text that appears on your web page by selecting <strong>View</strong> and <strong>Text size</strong> from the top menu in your browser. You will be given the following five options:</p>
<ul>
<li>Largest</li>
<li>Larger</li>
<li>Medium</li>
<li>Smaller</li>
<li>Smallest</li>
</ul>
<p>Simply click one of these options to select a font size.</p>
<p>Alternatively, you could scroll your mouse wheel while holding down the Ctrl key on your keyboard.</p>
<h3>Changing the colour of your screen</h3>
<p>If you are colour-blind or struggle with certain colour combinations, you can change the colour of your screen and text.</p>
<!-- TODO: is <strong> the best element for highlighting instructions -->
<!-- TODO: Reword as use of > will not be good for screen readers -->
<p>Click <strong>Tools</strong> in the top menu on your screen &gt; Select <strong>Internet options</strong> from the drop down menu &gt; Select the <strong>General</strong> tab &gt; Under <strong>Appearance</strong> you will see an option called <strong>Colors</strong>. Clicking this will allow you to change your colours to whatever combination you choose.</p>